-- Perceus-style explicit reference-count insertion for Core JSON.
--
-- The port owns branch and compiled-match balancing, repeated-context
-- protection, mutable reassignment, borrowed return and aggregate retention,
-- consumed-parameter balancing, and recursive final-drop insertion. Contract
-- inference (the reverse-parameter-flow graph, its solver, and call-site
-- annotation) is its own `ownership_contracts` Core pass that runs
-- immediately before this one and publishes `OwnershipContractFacts` on
-- `CorePassState`; `insert_drops_program` reads `facts.env` rather than
-- building the environment or solving the graph itself. Production
-- compilation enters Blorp after Core DCE and runs this pass before reuse,
-- closure conversion, resource lowering, and C emission.
